# Description: CHANGE REFERENCE DATA (change a PIN) - WRITE operation, edit first.
# Category: templates
#
# !!! THIS IS A WRITE OPERATION - IT PERMANENTLY CHANGES THE CARD !!!
# CHANGE REFERENCE DATA replaces the PIN (or another secret) stored on the
# card. A mistake here leaves you with a PIN you do not know, and wrong
# attempts count against the retry counter exactly as they do for VERIFY.
# Do not run this against a card you are not free to modify.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# Template that replaces the current PIN with new PIN data. Many cards
# expect the data as "current PIN block || new PIN block"; with 8-byte PIN
# blocks that means 16 data bytes and Lc = 10. The line below shows the
# single-block form (Lc = 08) used by cards that only want the new PIN
# block - check your card's manual to learn which form it expects, then
# EDIT BEFORE USE.
#
# THE COMMAND, BYTE BY BYTE
#   00                     class byte: standard interindustry commands
#   24                     instruction: CHANGE REFERENCE DATA
#   00                     P1 = 0: change, without unblocking
#   81                     P2: key reference 0x81 (PLACEHOLDER)
#   08                     Lc: 8 data bytes follow (10 for two blocks)
#   31 32 33 34 FF FF FF FF
#                          PLACEHOLDER data: PIN digits "1234" right-padded
#                          with FF (current PIN, or the NEW PIN block,
#                          depending on your card)
#
# WHAT YOU SHOULD SEE
#   SW 90 00               the reference data was changed
#   63 C X                 wrong current PIN, X attempts remain
#   63 C0 / 69 83          the PIN is now blocked
00 24 00 81 08 31 32 33 34 FF FF FF FF
